Inside a describe block an arrow callback sees the file's this, which is why helpers written as arrows cannot reach the fixture object they are nested in.

arguments is filled in by the engine the same way this is, and an arrow has no call of its own to be numbered. If you need the list of arguments, use a rest parameter instead.

code:
const rest = (...args) => args.length;
function normal() {
  return arguments.length;
}
console.log(rest(1, 2, 3));
console.log(normal(1, 2, 3));
try {
  const bad = () => arguments[0];
  console.log(bad());
} catch (err) {
  console.log(err.constructor.name);
}

