The prototype object is what new uses to look up inherited methods, and new is exactly what an arrow function refuses. A normal function also has prototype.constructor pointing back at itself.

code:
function normal() {}
const arrow = () => {};
console.log(normal.prototype.constructor === normal);
console.log(arrow.prototype);
console.log(typeof normal, typeof arrow);

