The arrow function was written outside the object literal, so its this is the surrounding file, not the object. The object property is just storage, it does not change which this an arrow looks at.

code:
const widget = {
  label: 'cart',
  bad: () => typeof this,
  good() {
    return this.label;
  },
};
console.log(widget.good());
console.log(widget.bad() === 'object' || widget.bad() === 'undefined');
const arrowAsMethod = widget.bad;
console.log(arrowAsMethod === widget.bad);

