Whenever you want more than one statement, or no return value, or an explicit return, or a block that declares its own variables. The braces also make the function body a normal block you can put new lines in.

code:
const short = (n) => n * 2;
const block = (n) => {
  const doubled = n * 2;
  return doubled + 1;
};
const silent = (n) => {
  n * 2;
};
console.log(short(2));
console.log(block(2));
console.log(silent(2));

