The parser reads a bare { after the arrow as the start of the function body, not as an object. Wrapping the object in parentheses makes it a single expression, so you can return it.

code:
const makeUser = (name) => ({ name, role: 'tester' });
const makeUserWithBody = (name) => {
  return { name, role: 'tester' };
};
console.log(makeUser('Ana'));
console.log(makeUserWithBody('Bo'));
console.log(typeof makeUser('Ana'));

