Playwright fixtures are often classes whose arrow fields hand you ready-to-run steps, which is the one place this pattern earns its keep.

The shorthand method is a normal function that happens to live on an object, so it gets its own this. The arrow gets the this of the file, which is almost never what the object method wants.

code:
const box = {
  value: 42,
  readMethod() {
    return this.value;
  },
  readArrow: () => 'no object this here',
};
console.log(box.readMethod());
console.log(box.readArrow());
console.log(typeof box.readMethod, typeof box.readArrow);

