The engine treats a bare expression after the arrow as an implicit return, which is why adding a second statement silently removes the value. This is the one place where the short form hides logic.

code:
const tax = (subtotal, rate) => Math.round(subtotal * rate * 100) / 100;
const taxWithBlock = (subtotal, rate) => {
  return Math.round(subtotal * rate * 100) / 100;
};
console.log(tax(100, 0.2));
console.log(taxWithBlock(100, 0.2));
console.log(tax.length, taxWithBlock.length);

