They are silently dropped, because an arrow has no arguments object to collect them in. The extra values only matter if you declared a rest parameter, and then they arrive as an array.

code:
const first = (a) => a;
console.log(first(1, 2, 3));
function second(a) {
  return [a, arguments.length];
}
console.log(second(1, 2, 3));
